From fcbfb801454e689bfe1b19b37cc8ebcdbf9b0cfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:17:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Wire staff/mock-ecommerce/case/warranty seeders into db:seed

Folds the seeders the handoff had you running manually
(StaffUserSeeder, CaseManagementSeeder, WarrantySeeder) plus
MockEcommerceSeeder into DatabaseSeeder::run(), in dependency order:

- StaffUserSeeder before CaseManagementSeeder/WarrantySeeder, since both
  pull from User::all() to assign a random staff member.
- MockEcommerceSeeder anywhere after Product/Customer/Order exist -- it's
  self-contained (firstOrCreate on its own demo customer/order), doesn't
  feed into or depend on anything around it.
- CaseManagementSeeder before WarrantySeeder, since WarrantySeeder now
  links claims back to existing cases for the same customer where one
  fits.

'php artisan db:seed' (after migrate:fresh) now does everything the
handoff's four separate commands used to.
---
 database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php b/database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php
index ad0260e..799e3da 100644
--- a/database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php
+++ b/database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php
@@ -7,6 +7,22 @@
 
 class DatabaseSeeder extends Seeder
 {
+    /**
+     * Order matters below, past the point ProductSeeder/CustomerSeeder/etc.
+     * finish:
+     *
+     * - StaffUserSeeder before CaseManagementSeeder/WarrantySeeder -- both
+     *   pull from User::all() to pick a random assignee, and want staff to
+     *   already exist rather than seeding zero-assignment demo data.
+     * - MockEcommerceSeeder can run any time after Product/Customer/Order
+     *   exist -- it only firstOrCreate()s its own standalone demo
+     *   customer/order for the mock e-commerce trigger form, so it doesn't
+     *   depend on or feed into the seeders around it.
+     * - CaseManagementSeeder before WarrantySeeder -- WarrantySeeder links
+     *   claims back to existing cases for the same customer where one
+     *   fits (mirrors what CaseController::store does for real requests),
+     *   so it needs cases to already exist to find a match.
+     */
     public function run(): void
     {
         // Mocked default user — until the real Users/Auth module is wired up,
@@ -20,10 +36,14 @@ public function run(): void
             ProductSeeder::class,
             CustomerSeeder::class,
             OrderSeeder::class,
-            HistoricalSalesOrderSeeder::class, 
+            HistoricalSalesOrderSeeder::class,
             PricingRuleSeeder::class,
             SalesQuotationSeeder::class,
             SalesOrderSeeder::class,
+            StaffUserSeeder::class,
+            MockEcommerceSeeder::class,
+            CaseManagementSeeder::class,
+            WarrantySeeder::class,
         ]);
     }
 }
